From 5eaa4e7e0d68473f80c7f6ee854811015769c6de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leeliu103 <liliu103@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:49:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [AMDGPU][Scheduler] Restore local spill rejection in
 occupancy mode (#233979)

When rematerializing for higher occupancy, the scheduler can retain a
schedule that introduces spills even when the saved order is spill-free.
The `!TargetOcc` guard disables local spill rejection. Since occupancy
is tracked using `max(WavesBefore, WavesAfter)`, global finalization can
still consider the target reached even when the trial schedule is worse.

The guard was introduced in 7cc7a9412893 (#180646) alongside a fix for
rollback using temporary `DBG_VALUE` placeholders. dc34d163d8c9
(#192443) replaced that representation with the shared MIR
rematerializer, removing the placeholder-specific slot-index issue.

Re-enable the existing `mayCauseSpilling` check in occupancy mode to
reject such trials and restore the instruction order saved before
rescheduling, while preserving rematerialization. Global finalization
still handles rematerialization rollback. Add a MIR regression that
spills before the fix and remains spill-free afterward.

Related Q2_K spilling discussion:
https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/29910

---------

Co-authored-by: leeliu103 <211733494+leeliu103@users.noreply.github.com>
